        <!--
            Engine damage smoke: the model replacement of the sim-driven stock EngineDamage effect (fx_engsmoke, the
            default when aircraft.cfg has no EngineDamage key), which aircraft.cfg turns off (EngineDamage = fx_dummy)
            because the flyPad "Situation Visual Effects" switch cannot reach a sim-driven effect.
            - Trigger (design choice): the SDK documents EngineDamage only as "Engine damage. Default would be
              fx_engsmoke" (aircraft.cfg [EFFECTS]), with no variable. ENG FAILED:n, the SDK's "failure flag for the
              indexed engine that has failed" (set by the engine failure of the MSFS failures menu; FBW code never writes
              it), is the engine damage state the user can reach. GENERAL ENG DAMAGE PERCENT:n is not used: any
              threshold on that percentage would be invented.
            - Not while the engine burns: the fire smoke (ENGINE_FIRE_FX above) is already there, one smoke per engine.
            - Look (design choice): the stock FX_Smoke_Fire graph of the fire smoke, same full-scale engine node, no
              offset.
            - ANDed with L:A32NX_CONFIG_SITUATION_FX like every situation effect. EngineFireEffects.spec.ts checks it.
        -->
