        <!--
            Engine oil leak smoke: the model replacement of the sim-driven stock EngineOilLeak effect (fx_OilLeak), which
            aircraft.cfg turns off (EngineOilLeak = fx_dummy) because the flyPad "Situation Visual Effects" switch cannot
            reach a sim-driven effect.
            - Trigger (design choice): the FBW oil leak itself, the condition under which the FADEC takes the oil out of
              the engine (fadec_common EngineOilFailures.hpp leakedQuantity): the flyPad oil leak failure
              (L:A32NX_ENGINE_n_OIL_LEAK, failures 79000/79001), the core turning the oil pump (L:A32NX_ENGINE_N2:n at
              10 % or more) and oil left in the oil system (L:A32NX_ENGINE_OIL_TOTAL:n above 0). No oil flows out of a
              stopped or emptied engine, so no smoke then. No exterior sign of an oil leak is documented.
            - Look (design choice): smoke, as the stock fx_OilLeak (fs-base-effects-legacy effects/fx_OilLeak.fx: grey-blue
              and black smoke particles; no MSFS 2024 visual effect graph or SDK template exists for an oil leak). The
              graph is the stock FX_Smoke_Fire of the fire and damage smoke, same full-scale engine node, no offset.
            - One smoke per engine: not while the engine burns (ENGINE_FIRE_FX smoke) or is failed (ENGINE_DAMAGE_FX).
            - ANDed with L:A32NX_CONFIG_SITUATION_FX like every situation effect. EngineFireEffects.spec.ts checks it.
        -->
